# Security and data

- Never write real tokens, passwords, or cloud keys into the repo. Use `.env` locally (gitignored) and GitHub Actions secrets in CI.
- Block commits of `*.tif` / `*.pt` / checkpoints unless the user explicitly wants a tiny fixture under `tests/fixtures/`.
- Treat user queries and uploaded scenes as sensitive. Do not log raw coordinates, user identity, or full prompts in production paths.
- Do not scrape or redistribute copyrighted satellite products. Prefer licensed ISRO/open datasets the team names explicitly.
- If a command would force-push, reset hard, or clean untracked files, stop and ask.
